      "text": "To solve the problem, we start by defining the positive integers \\(A\\), \\(B\\), \\(C\\), and \\(D\\) in terms of a variable \\(x\\). The given equations are:\n\n\\[A + 2 = B - 2 = C \\times 2 = D \\div 2 = x\\]\n\nThis means we can express \\(A\\), \\(B\\), \\(C\\), and \\(D\\) as follows:\n\\[A = x - 2\\]\n\\[B = x + 2\\]\n\\[C = \\frac{x}{2}\\]\n\\[D = 2x\\]\n\nWe also know that the sum of these four integers is 36:\n\\[A + B + C + D = 36\\]\n\nSubstituting the expressions for \\(A\\), \\(B\\), \\(C\\), and \\(D\\) into the sum equation, we get:\n\\[(x - 2) + (x + 2) + \\frac{x}{2} + 2x = 36\\]\n\nSimplifying the left side:\n\\[x - 2 + x + 2 + \\frac{x}{2} + 2x = 36\\]\n\\[4x + \\frac{x}{2} = 36\\]\n\nTo eliminate the fraction, we multiply every term by 2:\n\\[8x + x = 72\\]\n\\[9x = 72\\]\n\\[x = 8\\]\n\nNow we can find the values of \\(A\\), \\(B\\), \\(C\\), and \\(D\\):\n\\[A = x - 2 = 8 - 2 = 6\\]\n\\[B = x + 2 = 8 + 2 = 10\\]\n\\[C = \\frac{x}{2} = \\frac{8}{2} = 4\\]\n\\[D = 2x = 2 \\times 8 = 16\\]\n\nThe product \\(A \\times B \\times C \\times D\\) is:\n\\[A \\times B \\times C \\times D = 6 \\times 10 \\times 4 \\times 16\\]\n\nWe can calculate this step by step:\n\\[6 \\times 10 = 60\\]\n\\[60 \\times 4 = 240\\]\n\\[240 \\times 16 = 3840\\]\n\nThus, the value of the product \\(A \\times B \\times C \\times D\\) is \\(\\boxed{3840}\\).",
